ng 8 jobs' with all cards.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-7\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Search 'FIGMA' matched skill 'Figma' (job-2); 'techcorp' matched company name (job-1, job-2); 'nurse' matched title 'Registered Nurse' (job-3); results and count updated immediately and case-insensitively in each case.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-8\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Submitted application with name, valid email, phone, message on job-1; toast notification 'Application submitted! Your application for Senior Frontend Developer at TechCorp Solutions has been sent.' appeared and form reset.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-18\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"No edit functionality exists for published jobs\", \"actual\": \"Searched the employer dashboard (only 'view applications' and delete/trash icon buttons present per job row) and the job details page (no employer controls, only the application form) for an edit affordance; none exists. There is no way to modify a published job's details anywhere in the UI.\", \"evidence\": \"Employer dashboard job rows expose only an applications-count button and a trash/delete icon button; job detail pages show only the public view with an application form, no edit controls.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-9\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Empty submit blocked by required-field validation (Please fill out this field on Name/Email/Message). Invalid email 'not-an-email' blocked with native validation message identifying the Email field ('Please include an @ in the email address'). No application was created in either case.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-10\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Job posting form does not enforce required-skill or valid-salary-range constraints\", \"actual\": \"Posted 'QA Automation Engineer' with title/industry/type/location/description/salary filled but zero required skills added — job was published successfully with no error ('Job posted successfully!', 0 skills). Separately posted 'Salary Test Role' with Minimum Salary=150000 and Maximum Salary=50000 (min > max) — job was published successfully showing '$150k - $50k' with no validation error.\", \"evidence\": \"Employer dashboard shows both jobs live: 'QA Automation Engineer' with no skill tags and 0 applications, and 'Salary Test Role' listed as 'New York, NY · $150k - $50k · Posted Yesterday'.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-11\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Duplicate application with an already-used email is accepted instead of rejected\", \"actual\": \"Submitted a second application to job-1 using the same email (jamie.rivera@example.com) already used for that job. The app showed the same 'Application submitted!' success toast and the employer dashboard now lists both 'Jamie Rivera' and 'Jamie Rivera Duplicate' as two separate applications with the identical email, instead of blocking the second submission and leaving the original unchanged.\", \"evidence\": \"Employer dashboard Applications(4) list for Senior Frontend Developer shows both 'Jamie Rivera Duplicate' and 'Jamie Rivera' entries with email jamie.rivera@example.com.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-13\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Visible toast confirmation shown on submit; 'Jamie Rivera' application appears exactly once under Senior Frontend Developer in employer dashboard with matching name, email, phone, and message.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-14\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Each filter change immediately updated result count and cards (8→2→1→0), showed no-results empty state, and Clear filters immediately restored all 8 jobs.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-19\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Published jobs and submitted applications do not persist after a page reload\", \"actual\": \"After posting two new jobs (QA Automation Engineer, Salary Test Role) and submitting an application (Jamie Rivera) which were all visible in the dashboard/listings, reloading the app (revisiting the site) reset the data back to the original seed state: only the original 8 jobs remain ('Showing 8 jobs'), and the newly posted jobs and application are gone.\", \"evidence\": \"Home page after reload shows 'Showing 8 jobs' (job-1..job-8 only), no 'QA Automation Engineer' or 'Salary Test Role'.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-15\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Job cards on home listing (e.g. job-1) show title, company, industry badge, employment-type badge, location, salary range, posting date, and required skill tags.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-16\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"job-1 details page shows title, company, industry, employment type, location, salary range, 'Posted Jan 15' date, full description with responsibilities/requirements, and required skills list.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-17\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Each application card in the employer dashboard shows applicant name, email, optional phone (shown when provided, e.g. 555-9876/555-0101, omitted for Jamie Rivera Duplicate who didn't submit one), message text, and a submission date (e.g. 'Yesterday', 'Jan 20', 'Jan 22'), each as a distinct record.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-20\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Newly created jobs/applications show 'Yesterday' instead of 'Today' as submission/posting date\", \"actual\": \"Browser date confirmed as 2026-08-24 (today). A job posted seconds earlier shows 'Posted Yesterday' on both the employer dashboard and job listing card, and an application submitted moments earlier shows 'Yesterday' in the employer's applications list, instead of 'Today'.\", \"evidence\": \"'QA Automation Engineer' and 'Salary Test Role' both show 'Posted Yesterday'; Jamie Rivera application shows 'Yesterday' immediately after submission.\"}]}"
